{"total_count":1705,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32816","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32816/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32816/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32816/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/32816","id":4723662893,"node_id":"PR_kwDOC4Q8Qs7piCIq","number":32816,"title":"feat(source-control): add push endpoint to public API v1","user":{"login":"jjnyn","id":46193318,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MTkzMzE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46193318?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjnyn","html_url":"https://github.com/jjnyn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjnyn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjnyn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjnyn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjnyn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjnyn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjnyn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjnyn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjnyn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jjnyn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1417801476,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDE3ODAxNDc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/core","name":"core","color":"DC143C","default":false,"description":"Enhancement outside /nodes-base and /editor-ui"},{"id":3644139485,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs7ZNSfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/community","name":"community","color":"FF1493","default":false,"description":"Authored by a community member"},{"id":5015690190,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABKvVbzg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/in%20linear","name":"in linear","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"DEPRECATED"},{"id":9540479235,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOKgpAw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/triage:complete","name":"triage:complete","color":"FBCA04","default":false,"description":"Triage has been completed and issue is ready for internal teams"},{"id":9542227923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLX0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:team-assigned","name":"status:team-assigned","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"A team has been assigned the issue or PR"},{"id":10918344549,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACisi3ZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/cla-signed","name":"cla-signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11791216183,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACvs-uNw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/triage:ready-for-review","name":"triage:ready-for-review","color":"FBCA04","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2026-06-23T07:38:00Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T07:35:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/pulls/32816","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/32816","diff_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/32816.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/32816.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nDescribe what the PR does.\r\nPhotos and videos are recommended.\r\n-->\r\n- Adds `POST /api/v1/source-control/push` authenticated via `X-N8N-API-KEY`,\r\n  as a symmetric counterpart to the existing pull endpoint\r\n- Adds `GET /api/v1/source-control/status` to preview the set of changes that a\r\n  push (or pull) would include, without modifying anything. Returns a list of\r\n  `SourceControlledFile` objects — the same shape push accepts in `fileNames`\r\n- Accepts optional `fileNames` field (an array of `SourceControlledFile`\r\n  objects, typically obtained from the status endpoint) for pushing a specific\r\n  subset; falls back to all eligible files if omitted\r\n- Adds `sourceControl:push` as a valid `ApiKeyScope` available to owner/admin\r\n  API keys. `status` is authorised per direction (`direction=push` requires\r\n  `sourceControl:push`, `direction=pull` requires `sourceControl:pull`)\r\n\r\n### Integration flow\r\n\r\n```\r\nGET  /api/v1/source-control/status?direction=push   → diff of what would be pushed\r\n         ↓  (integration inspects / filters / approves)\r\nPOST /api/v1/source-control/push { fileNames: [...selected...] }   → push that subset\r\n```\r\n\r\nTwo supported modes:\r\n- **Push everything** — omit `fileNames`; the server computes the full eligible\r\n  change set. The push response echoes back `files`, so you get a receipt of\r\n  what was pushed.\r\n- **Selective / preview-then-push** — call status first, then push only the\r\n  chosen files.\r\n\r\n## How to test\r\nRequires a licensed instance connected to a source control repository, and an\r\nowner/admin API key.\r\n\r\n1. **Preview the diff**\r\n   ```\r\n   curl -H \"X-N8N-API-KEY: <key>\" \\\r\n     \"https://<instance>/api/v1/source-control/status?direction=push\"\r\n   ```\r\n2. **Push everything**\r\n   ```\r\n   curl -X POST -H \"X-N8N-API-KEY: <key>\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\r\n     -d '{\"commitMessage\":\"Automated backup\"}' \\\r\n     \"https://<instance>/api/v1/source-control/push\"\r\n   ```\r\n3. **Push a selected subset** — pass file objects from step 1 as `fileNames`.\r\n\r\nVerify: unlicensed → 401, licensed-but-not-connected → 400, missing/invalid key\r\n→ 401, insufficient scope → 403, conflicts (without `force`) → 409.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Related Linear tickets, Github issues, and Community forum posts\r\n- Community feature request: https://community.n8n.io/t/feat-source-control-add-push-endpoint-to-public-api-v1/277063\r\n<!--\r\nInclude links to **Linear ticket** or Github issue or Community forum post.\r\nImportant in order to close *automatically* and provide context to reviewers.\r\nhttps://linear.app/n8n/issue/[TICKET-ID]\r\n-->\r\n<!-- Use \"closes #<issue-number>\", \"fixes #<issue-number>\", or \"resolves #<issue-number>\" to automatically close issues when the PR is merged. -->\r\n\r\n\r\n## Review / Merge checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] I have seen this code, I have run this code, and I take responsibility for this code.\r\n- [x] PR title and summary are descriptive. ([conventions](../blob/master/.github/pull_request_title_conventions.md)) <!--\r\n   **Remember, the title automatically goes into the changelog.\r\n   Use `(no-changelog)` otherwise.**\r\n-->\r\n- [x] [Docs updated](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n-docs) or follow-up ticket created.\r\n- [x] Tests included. <!--\r\n   A bug is not considered fixed, unless a test is added to prevent it from happening again.\r\n   A feature is not complete without tests.\r\n-->\r\n- [x] PR Labeled with `Backport to Beta`, `Backport to Stable`, or `Backport to v1` (if the PR is an urgent fix that needs to be backported)\r\n\r\n\r\n<!-- stage-review-badge-begin -->\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://stagereview.app/n8n-io/n8n/pull/32816\">\r\n  <picture>\r\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://stagereview.app/assets/gh-open-in-stage-dark.svg\">\r\n    <img src=\"https://stagereview.app/assets/gh-open-in-stage-light.svg\" alt=\"Open in Stage\">\r\n  </picture>\r\n</a>\r\n\r\n<!-- stage-review-badge-end -->\r\n\r\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\r\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/n8n-io/n8n/pull/32816?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\r\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32816/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/32816/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/35905","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/35905/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/35905/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/35905/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/35905","id":5105923589,"node_id":"PR_kwDOC4Q8Qs78yu9g","number":35905,"title":"refactor(core): Move data-table source control handling into the data-table module","user":{"login":"CharlieKolb","id":13814565,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODE0NTY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13814565?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CharlieKolb","html_url":"https://github.com/CharlieKolb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CharlieKolb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CharlieKolb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CharlieKolb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CharlieKolb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CharlieKolb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CharlieKolb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CharlieKolb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CharlieKolb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CharlieKolb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":1417801476,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDE3ODAxNDc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/core","name":"core","color":"DC143C","default":false,"description":"Enhancement outside /nodes-base and /editor-ui"},{"id":3644142434,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs7ZNTNi","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/n8n%20team","name":"n8n team","color":"ffffff","default":false,"description":"Authored by the n8n team"},{"id":10918344549,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACisi3ZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/cla-signed","name":"cla-signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-08-10T02:02:04Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T02:30:25Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/pulls/35905","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/35905","diff_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/35905.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/35905.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\nRemoves the `source-control.ee` → `data-table` half of the remaining cross-module dependency cycle between backend modules.\n\n- `source-control.ee` gains a narrow seam: a `SourceControlDataTableHandler` interface (export files, remote/local status listing, import/apply, deletion, remote-project resolution) and a `@Service()` `SourceControlResourceHandlerRegistry`.\n- The data-table specific export/import/status logic moves wholesale into `packages/cli/src/modules/data-table/source-control/data-table-source-control.service.ts`, which implements the handler and is registered during `DataTableModule.init()` (mirroring the existing `OwnershipTransferHandlerRegistry` pattern).\n- The two queries that needed TypeORM operators moved behind use-case methods on `DataTableRepository` (`findForSourceControlExport`, `findForSourceControlStatus`) so the new service stays free of `@n8n/typeorm` imports — no additions to the lint ratchet allowlist.\n- `SourceControlScopedService` no longer references the `DataTable` entity; the data-table filter is built inside the data-table module from the public `getProjectsWithPushScopeByContextFilter`.\n- The core resource types (workflows, credentials, variables, tags, folders, projects) stay inline as before — no generalization.\n\nBehavior is unchanged: exported file names/formats, import ordering, and validation semantics are identical (code was moved, not rewritten). The only intentional difference: if the data-table module is inactive (both modules are defaults, so this is theoretical), source control now cleanly skips the resource type instead of failing at query time against unregistered entities.\n\nData-table-specific tests were relocated from the source-control test files into `src/modules/data-table/source-control/__tests__/`; source-control tests now mock the handler through the registry.\n\n## How to test\n\n- `pnpm test src/modules/source-control.ee` and `pnpm test src/modules/data-table` in `packages/cli` (all passing).\n- Integration: `pnpm test:integration test/integration/environments/source-control*.test.ts` (all passing; the suite exercises data-table push/pull/status end-to-end).\n- Manually: connect source control, push and pull an instance containing data tables; the `datatables/*.json` files and pull results are byte-identical to before.\n\n## Related Linear tickets, Github issues, and Community forum posts\n\nPart of https://linear.app/n8n/issue/DEVP-646\n\n## Review / Merge checklist\n\n- [x] I have seen this code, I have run this code, and I take responsibility for this code.\n- [x] PR title and summary are descriptive. ([conventions](../blob/master/.github/pull_request_title_conventions.md))\n- [ ] [Docs updated](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n-docs) or follow-up ticket created.\n- [x] Tests included.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/n8n-io/n8n/pull/35905?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/35905/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/35905/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/35925","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/35925/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/35925/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/35925/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/35925","id":5108243849,"node_id":"PR_kwDOC4Q8Qs786Enh","number":35925,"title":"build(editor): Resolve @n8n/tournament from source via the n8n:source condition (no-changelog)","user":{"login":"alexgrozav","id":6179477,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNzk0Nzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6179477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav","html_url":"https://github.com/alexgrozav","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexgrozav/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":3644142434,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs7ZNTNi","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/n8n%20team","name":"n8n team","color":"ffffff","default":false,"description":"Authored by the n8n team"},{"id":10918344549,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACisi3ZQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/cla-signed","name":"cla-signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-08-10T08:38:51Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T09:00:19Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/pulls/35925","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/35925","diff_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/35925.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/pull/35925.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\n`@n8n/tournament` now declares its own frontend resolution in its `package.json`, and editor-ui's\nhand-maintained alias for it is gone.\n\n```jsonc\n// packages/@n8n/tournament/package.json\n\"exports\": { \".\": { \"n8n:source\": \"./src/index.ts\", /* …unchanged… */ } }\n```\n\n```ts\n// packages/frontend/editor-ui/vite.config.mts\nresolve: { alias, conditions: resolveConditions }   // ['n8n:source', ...defaultClientConditions]\n```\n\nWhy this package first: it is the one entry in editor-ui's alias list that exists purely to fix a\n**transitive** dependency. `n8n-workflow`'s built ESM imports `astVisit` from tournament, whose\n`dist` is CJS — linked workspace packages skip `optimizeDeps`, so the dev server serves that file\nverbatim and the browser cannot parse a named export out of it, while the production build survives\nonly because rolldown interops CJS, at a cost of ~397 kB in defeated tree-shaking. An alias in\neditor-ui cannot express that, because editor-ui never imports the package: it is a false negative\nfor any consumer-side mapping, generated or hand-written. Declaring the source entry on the package\nitself puts the fact where the fact belongs, and any Vite context that opts into the condition\ninherits the fix.\n\nThe spread in `resolveConditions` is load-bearing: `conditions` **replaces** Vite's defaults rather\nthan appending to them, so dropping it would silently change third-party resolution across the whole\ngraph. A test pins the exact array for that reason.\n\n### Verification\n\nTypecheck-green and build-green are known-insufficient for this package — the ~397 kB regression was\ninvisible to both — so every claim below has a negative control that fires.\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Vite **dev server** in Chromium | Serves `tournament/src/index.ts` + 7 more `src/*.ts`, all 200, zero `dist` requests; `astVisit` is a live `function`; `expression-sandboxing.js` loads clean |\n| ↳ negative control (condition removed) | App fails to boot: `The requested module '…/tournament/dist/index.js' does not provide an export named 'astVisit'` — verbatim the documented failure |\n| Production bundle | 45,110,584 B with the condition vs **45,507,890 B** with no resolution config → **−397,306 B**, matching the previously measured regression byte-for-byte |\n| ↳ attribution | With the condition, `astVisit` is tree-shaken out entirely (0 chunks) and 3 chunks reference `tournament/src`; without it, 3 chunks reference `tournament/dist` |\n| `vue-tsc` honours `customConditions`? | **Yes** — 2.2.8 / TS 6.0.2, in `.ts` and inside a `.vue` SFC alike; control without the option resolves `dist` and errors (exit 2). See \"Not changed\" below for why none is added here |\n| Backend resolution | Unchanged and structurally so: default Node ESM `import.meta.resolve` and CJS `require.resolve` both still land on `dist`; only an explicit opt-in reaches `src` |\n| editor-ui typecheck / build / unit suite | Green |\n\nThe two repo assertions in `vite/aliases.test.ts` resolve `@n8n/tournament` through a **real Vite\nserver**, not a model of one, and were mutation-tested: deleting the condition from the package\nfails the positive case with `expected 'packages/@n8n/tournament/dist/index.js' to be\n'packages/@n8n/tournament/src/index.ts'`, and dropping the spread fails the defaults case. This\nmatters because the failure mode is silent by construction — a wrong condition falls back to `dist`\ninstead of erroring.\n\nThe old alias-based `resolves @n8n/tournament from source` case is replaced by those two, since the\nalias it asserted on no longer exists. Its second half also asserted a subpath (`@n8n/tournament/ast`)\nthat nothing imports — all five importers in the repo use the bare specifier — so a `\".\"` entry is\nthe whole requirement here and no extension-specific `\"./src/*.ts\"` pattern is needed.\n\n### Not changed, deliberately\n\n- **No `customConditions` on any tsconfig, and no `paths` key was deleted — there was none.** No\n  frontend TypeScript context resolves this package: `vue-tsc --listFiles` puts 8,008 files in\n  editor-ui's program and tournament is not among them, because the `.d.ts` chain reachable from\n  `n8n-workflow`'s entry never references it (only `expression-sandboxing.d.ts` does, and nothing\n  imports that subpath). Adding a global resolution option whose effect is unobservable would be\n  scaffolding, not safety. When the six frontend-only packages gain the condition they *are* in that\n  program, and that is when editor-ui's tsconfig needs `customConditions` — testably.\n- **Storybook.** `@n8n/storybook`'s Vite context has no equivalent alias, so this chain breaks its\n  dev server today — see the comment at `ToolsConnectionModal.stories.ts:108`. Pre-existing, not\n  touched here; it is a candidate beneficiary of the condition and belongs with the deferred-consumer\n  work rather than this PR.\n- The four other frontend packages that declare `n8n-workflow` (`@n8n/composables`, `@n8n/stores`,\n  `@n8n/rest-api-client`, `@n8n/i18n`) — their suites pass as-is; no opt-in added without a\n  demonstrated need.\n\n## How to test\n\n```bash\npnpm --filter n8n-editor-ui vitest run vite/aliases.test.ts   # 20 passing\npnpm --filter n8n-editor-ui typecheck\npnpm --filter n8n-editor-ui build\npnpm --filter n8n-editor-ui dev                               # then load the editor\n```\n\nTo see the mechanism doing the work, delete `\"n8n:source\"` from\n`packages/@n8n/tournament/package.json` and reload the dev server: the app stops booting with\n`does not provide an export named 'astVisit'`, and the tests go red.\n\n## Sequencing\n\n**Branched from #35642, not from `master`** — that PR introduces `vite/aliases.mts` and\n`aliases.test.ts`, the single source of alias truth this change edits, and it is still open with\n`CHANGES_REQUESTED`. Basing on `master` would mean re-landing a conflicting version of that mapping.\nThis PR should land after it; the diff against #35642 is the four files above.\n\nThis is the first, smallest step of the direction agreed for frontend source resolution: resolution\ntruth moves into each package's own `package.json` instead of being mirrored in consumer-side lists.\nIt changes no published artifact — tournament already ships `src/` in `files`, and `n8n:source` is\ninert unless a consumer opts in.\n\n## Review / Merge checklist\n\n- [x] I have seen this code, I have run this code, and I take responsibility for this code.\n- [x] PR title and summary are descriptive. ([conventions](../blob/master/.github/pull_request_title_conventions.md))\n- [ ] [Docs updated](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n-docs) or follow-up ticket created.\n- [x] Tests included.\n- [ ] PR Labeled with `Backport to Beta`, `Backport to Stable`, or `Backport to v1` (if the PR is an urgent fix that needs to be backported)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/n8n-io/n8n/pull/35925?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Review in cubic\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/35925/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/35925/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34292","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34292/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34292/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34292/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34292","id":4898550480,"node_id":"I_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABI_ny0A","number":34292,"title":"Source control push does not detect \"Available in MCP\" workflow setting change","user":{"login":"Marshall-Qiu","id":89381510,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MzgxNTEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89381510?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu","html_url":"https://github.com/Marshall-Qiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9542225587,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLOsw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:in-linear","name":"status:in-linear","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Issue or PR is now in Linear"},{"id":9542227923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLX0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:team-assigned","name":"status:team-assigned","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"A team has been assigned the issue or PR"},{"id":10081993897,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACWO8EqQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/team:lifecycle","name":"team:lifecycle","color":"7A36AC","default":false,"description":"Issue is with the Lifecycle & Governance team"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-07-16T04:00:40Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T15:42:14Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Bug Description\n\nWhen a workflow's **\"Available in MCP\"** setting is the *only* thing changed, the source-control push modal does not list the workflow as modified, so the change cannot be pushed to the protected/remote instance.\n\nAs a workaround I currently have to make an additional (unwanted) edit to a node/connection just so the workflow shows up as pushable — which also pushes that unwanted change.\n\n**Root cause (from source):** Source control determines whether a workflow changed by comparing only `versionId`, `parentFolderId`, and `owner` (`isWorkflowModified` in `packages/cli/src/modules/source-control.ee/source-control-helper.ee.ts:459`). The \"Available in MCP\" toggle is stored inside the workflow `settings` object (`availableInMCP` — `packages/workflow/src/interfaces.ts:3620`) and a settings-only change does **not** generate a new `versionId` (`packages/cli/src/services/workflow.service.ts:412`, and the bulk toggle path `packages/cli/src/modules/mcp/mcp.settings.service.ts:207`). The exported workflow file *does* include the full `settings` object (`source-control-export.service.ee.ts:137`), but the status comparison never diffs file content — so the change is invisible to the push modal.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. On an instance connected to source control (environments), with a workflow already committed/pushed.\n2. Open the workflow and toggle **Available in MCP** (in Workflow Settings, or via the MCP settings/card toggle) — change nothing else.\n3. Open the source control **Push** modal.\n4. The workflow is **not** listed as changed, so the setting change cannot be pushed.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nA change to \"Available in MCP\" (and, more generally, any workflow `settings` change) should mark the workflow as modified so it appears in the push modal and can be pushed on its own.\n\n### n8n Version\n\n2.26.3\n\n### Database\n\nN/A — logic bug, reproducible on any DB\n\n### Execution Mode\n\nN/A\n\n### Hosting\n\nSelf-hosted (source control / environments is an Enterprise feature)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34292/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34292/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528/events","html_url":"https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528","id":4925479210,"node_id":"I_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAABJZTZKg","number":34528,"title":"Source control push panel does not show deleted tags as a change","user":{"login":"Marshall-Qiu","id":89381510,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MzgxNTEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89381510?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu","html_url":"https://github.com/Marshall-Qiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marshall-Qiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":9542225587,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLOsw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:in-linear","name":"status:in-linear","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Issue or PR is now in Linear"},{"id":9542227923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACOMLX0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/status:team-assigned","name":"status:team-assigned","color":"d93f0b","default":false,"description":"A team has been assigned the issue or PR"},{"id":10081993897,"node_id":"LA_kwDOC4Q8Qs8AAAACWO8EqQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/labels/team:lifecycle","name":"team:lifecycle","color":"7A36AC","default":false,"description":"Issue is with the Lifecycle & Governance team"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-07-20T03:17:55Z","updated_at":"2026-07-20T09:02:12Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Bug Description\n\nOn an instance connected to source control (Environments feature), deleting a tag is not surfaced as a pending change in the source control push panel. The deletion therefore never gets committed to the git repository, and instances that pull from the same repository keep the deleted tag indefinitely.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Set up two instances connected to the same source control repository (one push instance, one pull/protected instance), following the Environments docs.\n2. On the push instance, create a tag, assign it to a workflow, and push so `tags.json` in the repo contains it.\n3. On the push instance, delete the tag.\n4. Open the source control push panel (Commit and push).\n5. Observe: no pending change is listed for the deleted tag, so the deletion cannot be pushed. Pull instances continue to show the tag.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nDeleting a tag should appear as a `tags` change with status `deleted` in the push panel, and pushing should update `tags.json` in the repository so pull instances remove the tag as well.\n\n### Debug Info\n\nObserved on self-hosted 2.26.3 with the Environments/source control feature licensed and enabled, in a two-instance setup (build instance pushes, protected production instance pulls).\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux (Kubernetes)\n\n### n8n Version\n\n2.26.3\n\n### Node.js Version\n\n22.x\n\n### Database\n\nPostgreSQL\n\n### Execution Mode\n\nqueue\n\n### Hosting\n\nself hosted","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/n8n-io/n8n/issues/34528/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}